Design Report
Section 1. Project Scope and Design Priorities
1.1 Project Purpose
The project will develop a supplementary e-learning product that supports independent grammar application and written production within QiYao’s THINK program.
The design responds to findings from client meetings, teacher questionnaires, student assignments, textbook analysis, and course-placement results. Identified needs include complete sentence construction, grammatical accuracy, contextual grammar selection, task relevance, and reduced dependence on teacher prompts.
1.2 Project Scope
The curriculum framework will cover THINK Starter through Level 5. The product will include:
* Modules integrating related content across textbook units and levels.
* Age-responsive pathways for Grades 2–3 and Grades 4–5.
* Explicit grammar explanations and contextual examples.
* Sentence-construction and writing activities.
* Vocabulary and grammar reference resources.
* Self-checking practice, teacher-reviewed writing, and revision opportunities.
* Learner and teacher guidance.
The supplement will retain clear textbook connections while using its own prerequisite-based learning sequences. Existing classroom instruction will continue.
1.3 Development Priorities
Initial development will prioritize sentence construction and grammar-to-writing application in Starter and Level 1, where assignment evidence is currently available.
The first prototype will address personal-information responses using affirmative forms of be. Later development will extend to other modules following teacher review and formative evaluation.
The framework covers all six levels. Completion dates, release scope, budget, and production capacity require agreement with the client and management.
