The Nine Events will guide module experiences without requiring nine separate pages or a rigid sequence in every lesson. Events may extend across several short lessons within a module.
Section 3. Project Goals and Course Outcomes
3.1 Project Goals
The project aims to:
1. Establish a curriculum connecting grammar understanding, sentence construction, and writing development.
2. Define course outcomes and aligned assessment practices.
3. Provide two age-responsive pathways with adjustments for proficiency and writing readiness.
4. Support movement from guided practice to independent application.
5. Establish manageable self-checking, teacher feedback, and revision procedures.
6. Develop and evaluate a reusable module structure for expansion across the series.
Project success will be examined through instructional alignment, usability, implementation feasibility, and learner performance during formative evaluation.
Examination improvement and commercial adoption remain broader stakeholder expectations.
3.2 Shared Course Outcomes
After completing the relevant learning sequence, learners will be able to:
