6.3 **Proposed Student-learning Module Sequence
(update 5/3-5/6/2026)**
Structure and Pathway Application
The supplementary course will contain 90 provisionally defined learning modules, arranged in a continuous sequence.
Each module will provide:
                                    * A clear learning objective.
                                    * Brief review of required prior learning.
                                    * Contextualized explanation and examples.
                                    * Guided practice with feedback.
                                    * Independent application.
                                    * Checking and revision where relevant.
Both age pathways will use the same module sequence. Tasks, examples, scaffolding, and written-production requirements will be adapted for Grades 2–3 and Grades 4–5.
Learners will complete the agreed portion of the sequence appropriate to their readiness. The full series represents the product’s curriculum scope; it does not require every current elementary learner to complete advanced content immediately.
