	Section 7. Instructional Strategies and Learning Experience
7.1 Explanation and Application
Instruction will connect form, meaning, and use through contextual examples, sentence-part highlighting, meaningful contrasts, and guided construction.
Brief Chinese explanations may support difficult concepts or instructions where appropriate.
7.2 Age-Responsive Support
Grades 2–3
	Grades 4–5
	Concrete topics and visuals
	Context comparisons and model-text analysis
	Short instructions and smaller task sets
	Planning and organization procedures
	Optional oral rehearsal
	Sentence and paragraph revision
	Temporary word banks and sentence frames
	Guided choices among multiple structures
	Simple checking procedures
	More detailed self-review criteria
	These are starting approaches. Actual support will respond to performance evidence.
7.3 Reading–Grammar–Writing Connection
Short readings will demonstrate the target structures in meaningful use. Learners will identify how language expresses information, examine the sentence patterns, and apply them in their own responses.
Reading length and vocabulary will support the module’s purpose rather than introduce unnecessary demands.
