Section 10. Formative Evaluation and Revision Plan
10.1 Teacher Review
Teachers will review content accuracy, prerequisite assumptions, explanation clarity, task relevance, age appropriateness, and assessment criteria.
10.2 Learner Testing
A small group will test the prototype after necessary arrangements and parental permissions.
Selection will represent different sentence-writing abilities within the age pathways.
10.3 Evidence Collected
Evaluation will examine:
                                    * Understanding of instructions and explanations.
                                    * Navigation and submission.
                                    * Supported and independent performance.
                                    * Types of errors.
                                    * Completion time.
                                    * Use of feedback.
                                    * Teacher scoring consistency and workload.
10.4 Revision Decisions
Finding
	Design Response
	Instructions are misunderstood
	Simplify wording or add a demonstration
	Guided practice succeeds but independent performance remains weak
	Strengthen intermediate practice and examine prerequisite needs
	Task completion takes excessive time
	Reduce task load or divide lessons
	Learners repeatedly omit sentence elements
	Improve sentence-pattern explanations and construction practice
	Teachers score responses differently
	Clarify criteria and review sample responses together
	Feedback does not lead to correction
	Revise feedback and require a focused follow-up task
	The evaluated prototype will inform subsequent modules. Pilot findings will guide improvement without being treated as evidence of effectiveness across the entire series.
